<title>USA: FREE-TO-TRADE - Michigan $54.5 mln trunk line sale.</title>
<headline>FREE-TO-TRADE - Michigan $54.5 mln trunk line sale.</headline>
<text>
<p>STATE OF MICHIGAN</p>
<p>RE: $54,500,000</p>
<p>STATE TRUNK LINE FUND BONDS, SERIES 1996A</p>
<p>Effective immediately all syndicate terms and price restrictions are removed on the term bonds, and the bonds are now free to trade.</p>
<p>Morgan Stanley &amp; Co. Incorporated</p>
<p>Goldman, Sachs &amp; Co.</p>
<p>IN ASSOCIATION WITH:</p>
<p>J.P. Morgan Securities Inc.</p>
<p>Lehman Brothers</p>
<p>IN ASSOCIATION WITH:</p>
<p>First Chicago Capital Markets, Inc.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
